# EasyNet / Axon Commit Plan 2 — rev. 2026-06-12 (intraday update: Axis E executed)

## Revision Note

This revision rebaselines the 2026-06-05 plan against the repos as of
2026-06-12. Three structural shifts since the original baseline:

1. **RFC-005 landed.** The URA/namespace resolver train shipped across all
   three repos (Axon PR #27 merge `cd0a51b5`, CLI PR #22 merge `5d1a55e`,
   backend PR #20 merge `2c1118d`). Most of the original Axis A "DNS-like
   resolver" content is now description of reality, not plan.
2. **Receipt chain closure landed.** `easynet-verify` walks lifecycle and
   causal chains (offline bundle mode), causal links persist to the ledger by
   receipt hash, and EAL lowers exec steps to seven-tuple Invocations with
   receipt-chained causal context. Axis B is mostly done.
3. **The compatibility-window methodology is retired.** CTO standing
   directive: no backward-compat shims — prove canonical equivalence, then
   cut over cleanly (precedent: F-039 removed top-level `join/start/stop`
   aliases same-day, `a1a4aea`). All dual-name rollout machinery in the
   original plan is rewritten accordingly.

**Division of labor.** The `to-be-fix.md` / `to-be-fix.plan.md` /
`to-be-fix.spec.md` trio (live, 2026-06-12) owns the *debt plane*: problem
inventory, architectural diagnosis, and fix specs. This file owns the
*forward plan*: feature/release trains and sequencing. Debt items are
referenced here by their F-number / spec section and are NOT respecified;
single accounting lives in the trio.

## Purpose

This plan supersedes `commit-plan` as the execution plan after the daemon
Invocation migration. It folds in the 2026-06-02 product/user-case review
(`2026-06-02-015131-user-case.txt`): EasyNet must let a user discover,
trust, authorize, transact with, and audit stranger agents without knowing
the internal Axon/EAL/MCP machinery.

The remaining work has three axes:

1. **Naming / ontology cleanup** — now mostly reduced to the `<self>.*` /
   flat-verb migration, which is coupled to the SessionDispatch carrier
   unification (to-be-fix.spec §A2), not a standalone rename.
2. **Audit / capability completeness** — chain verification shipped; what
   remains is cross-process closure and hosted-agent signer binding.
3. **Product command-surface convergence** — still the largest open gap:
   intent-first discover, trust UX, and permission/policy UX do not exist.

