## Invariants

1. Axon owns protocol shape, canonical bytes, signatures, admission,
   receipts, stream/bidi semantics, verifier behavior, and cross-language
   SDK contracts.
2. EasyNet-Cli daemon owns product/device/Hub policy: local identity,
   keyring forwarding, plugins, EAL/Mission, local resources, sessions,
   device abilities, and Hub/device behavior. Hub now requires TLS.
3. EasyNet backend owns product surface: HTTP/API, browser UX, DB
   projections, auth/session UX, dashboards, and product aggregation.
4. Public callable surfaces collapse to Ability. Skill, plugin, tool,
   handler, raw RPC, HTTP endpoint, and gRPC method are implementation or
   transport details unless explicitly exposed as an Ability.
5. Every product invocation crossing a process or language boundary
   preserves the seven-tuple
   `caller, callee, ability, subject, nonce, causal_context, args -> receipt`.
   Status: implemented end-to-end for EAL exec steps (`ce8588e`, `04559af`,
   agent-grained callee `9a84a98`, ratified 2026-06-11).
6. JSON control remains boot/status/diagnostics only. Known violation:
   SessionDispatch business frames (F-004); closing it is the carrier
   unification (to-be-fix.spec §A2), not a relitigation of this invariant.
7. Ability family is projection metadata only. URA routing and Invocation
   stay flat.
8. Trust and permission are separate product questions.
9. Structure refactors preserve protocol behavior first.
10. **URA is owner-token-first.** The `axon-ura` crate is the single parser;
    grammar includes device-owned agents
    (`agent/device.<device-id>.<agent-id>`) and hosted-agent abilities
    addressed via their hosting device (`64190a6b`, `35efe641`). No
    application-layer URA fabrication (backend dropped client route hints,
    `09830a2`).
11. **Resolve before invoke.** Catalog/product reads and routing consume
    resolver answers; no owner inference from names.
12. **No compatibility windows.** Migrations prove canonical equivalence,
    then cut over. Aliases are deleted in the same change that proves
    equivalence (CTO directive; F-039 precedent).
13. **Single debt accounting.** Architecture/debt items live in the
    to-be-fix trio; this plan references, never duplicates.

