## Release Gates

### Gate A — Namespace Migration (rescoped)

- No active `<self>.*` ability names after cutover; lint enforces in the
  same change (no window).
- No flat daemon system verbs outside `device.*` / `hub.*`; `<user>.*` /
  `<agent>.*` owner-qualified names are registered with explicit OwnerKind.
- Friendly names and family projection never appear as routable identities
  in receipts.
- Historical receipt display renders legacy names read-only, without
  record rewriting.
- RFC-005 guards stay green: URA guard checks, resolver release profiles,
  resolve-before-invoke in backend.

### Gate B — Audit Closure (remainder)

- `easynet verify` validates a daemon-produced chain through a
  URA/hash-addressed fetch surface (not only pre-collected bundles).
- Backend receipt links audited as projections only.
- Hosted-agent receipts state callee, signer/host, and attestation
  distinctly, building on `authority_binding`; old self-signed receipts
  remain valid.

### Gate C — Runtime Boundary (unchanged + carrier)

- `scripts/check-daemon-invocation-migration.sh` stays green.
- No production caller constructs JSON control product frames.
- **SessionDispatch frames carry canonical Invocation shape after spec §A2
  lands; until then the violation is tracked, not re-litigated.**
- No Axon SDK API starts `easynet-daemon`; no backend code hosts device
  abilities; no CLI code defines canonical bytes or verification semantics.

### Gate D — User-Case Command Surface

- `easynet whoami` — shipped; keep green.
- `discover "<intent>"` returns local + federated candidates through one
  resolver-backed path.
- `trust` commands expose claims/anchors/sync state and do not imply
  authorization; `policy`/`permission` commands do not imply trust.
- Owner can grant/revoke/list permission for an ability or family scope;
  remote-desktop self-consent folds into the same model.
- `new-ability` import paths stay the single packaging model (no second
  ability model).
- Wallet/agreement/payment stays reserved until Axon owns settlement.

### Gate E — Structure Health

- Owned by to-be-fix.spec §A5 acceptance gates. This plan adds one rule:
  E1–E2 precede (or co-land with) any spec §A2 carrier change to
  `daemon_invocation_service.rs`.

